The basis file gives each row of the dataset its own public sources (source name, URL, date, quoted figure) and whether they agree with the row. Its bytes are bound here with the dataset's.

Previous release, cited and not edited:

    previous_version        2.2.0
    previous_dataset_sha256 85418e4af9d3d727af2eb1c95566aa56f21d8ae1046601bc259baa302515680d
    previous_dataset_url    https://shield.the-horizons-innovation.com/data/souba-db-2.2.0.json
    previous_anchor         jidec:entry:42 (claim_sha256 ac11efd49d231c0d0a4fa1e04930a8864d2670916dfad41c5868f01c66db5e03)

The previous bytes stay served at their own URL, so a verdict that cites the previous dataset_sha256 can still be recomputed against the bytes it names.

